{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01Vrk499FgDD6wPZfRgFET8k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Written and committed **Q12: Operational/business metrics: win rate, deflection rate, p95 latency** (`answers/05-012-operationalbusiness-metrics-win-rate-deflection-rate-p95-lat.md`).\n\nKey content:\n- **Three-bucket framework**: quality (win rate, deflection rate, CSAT, hallucination rate), efficiency (TTFT, p95/p99 latency), and business value (cost per query, cost per deflection)\n- **Concrete targets**: ≥70–80% deflection rate, <3s p95 for support bots, <$0.005 cost/query, <3% hallucination rate SLO\n- **Measurement pipeline**: structured per-call logging → async Kafka RAGAS sidecar → Grafana dashboards → PagerDuty alerting\n- **Key tradeoff**: deflection rate vs CSAT conflict — high deflection with bad answers tanks trust; set escalation triggers (cosine < 0.70 or faithfulness < 0.80) to balance them\n- **ROI framing**: $0.08 AI cost vs $8 human agent = 100× cost argument for executives\n- **3 pitfalls**: offline-only reporting, deflection as sole metric, average vs p95 latency\n\n12 of 23 questions complete for `05-evaluation-metrics`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":350,"cache_read_input_tokens":67429,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":350,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d4dffdf3-eb87-49f8-a661-c6fecbce0fd3","uuid":"be3a7fdc-11af-49d0-a758-8e246b691f01"}
